{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1791550916","published":"2026-10-12T11:23:31Z","modified":"2026-11-27T16:43:53.229035328Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-0672","CVE-2026-0864","CVE-2026-11940","CVE-2026-11972","CVE-2026-15308","CVE-2026-3644","CVE-2026-4224","CVE-2026-7210","CVE-2026-82049","CVE-2026-9669"],"summary":"python3.11: Fix of 11 CVEs","details":"- CVE-2026-0672: http.cookies: reject control characters in Morsel keys,\n  values and parameters so they cannot inject extra header lines\n- CVE-2026-4224: pyexpat: guard the recursion in conv_content_model() so a\n  deeply nested DTD content model raises RecursionError instead of overflowing\n  the C stack\n- CVE-2026-11940: tarfile: re-filter the member used for the hard-link\n  extraction fallback so a deeper symlink cannot be recreated outside the\n  destination\n- CVE-2026-11972: tarfile: stop _Stream.seek() at end of data so a truncated\n  stream raises ReadError instead of looping forever\n- CVE-2026-3644: http.cookies: reject control characters passed through\n  Morsel.update(), |=, pickling and js_output()\n- CVE-2026-0864: configparser: normalize CR, CRLF and LF line endings in\n  written values so a value cannot inject new sections or options\n- CVE-2026-9669: bz2: refuse to reuse a BZ2Decompressor after a decompression\n  error instead of resuming from an invalid internal state\n- CVE-2026-15308: html.parser: buffer incremental feed() input so unterminated\n  markup fed in small chunks is no longer parsed in quadratic time\n- CVE-2026-82049: tarfile: resolve the hard link target before linking so\n  that, with the data filter, a hard link to a symlink cannot recreate the\n  symlink outside the destination\n- CVE-2026-7210: seed the libexpat parser with 16 bytes of entropy via\n  XML_SetHashSalt16Bytes (bound as a weak symbol; falls back to the legacy\n  XML_SetHashSalt when unavailable), widening the hash salt from 8 to 16\n  bytes; with PYTHONHASHSEED=0 the zero hash secret now also reaches libexpat